    "axis": "does the ell-1 binding ceiling bound the family tr_M(. w), or only the single point w = 1 that the corpus reads?",
    "answer": "Only w = 1. The ceiling ranges over COEFFICIENTS at a fixed evaluation point and never varies the point. Every tr_M(x.w) is a Markov trace, hence a Hecke-trace object inside the N = 2 carrier and not row-capped, and the family's chi-vectors span the full partition space.",
